  "2019 P2 Q3": {"marks":4,"subject":"Reading an exchange rate from a graph; finding the date a given rate applied.","rows":[{"for":"read rate of exchange from graph","shows":"\\(0.852\\)","part":"(a)"},{"for":"calculate amount in pounds","shows":"\\(0.852 \\times 250 = 213\\)","part":"(a)"},{"for":"calculate exchange rate","shows":"\\(334.80 \\div 400 = 0.837\\) or \\(400 \\times 0.837 = 334.80\\)","part":"(b)"},{"for":"state date consistent with working","shows":"9 December","part":"(b)"}],"notes":["(a) 1. If •¹ is incorrect •² is not available for candidates who truncate or round their answer to a whole number of pounds.","(a) 2. •² is only available for candidates who multiply 250 by any value \\(0.83 \\le x \\le 0.86\\).","(b) 1. Correct answer with no working, award 0/2.","(b) 2. •⁴ is only available where calculated exchange rate is a marked point on the graph.","(b) 3. Where candidates choose to multiply, •⁴ is only available if the answer to one of their calculations is 334.80 and date is consistent with the exchange rate."]},
