  "2019 P2 Q7": {"marks":13,"subject":"Mean and standard deviation and two comparisons; a scattergraph, a line of best fit and an estimate; whether a pack of milk powder lasts a week.","rows":[{"for":"calculate mean","shows":"\\((2.5 + 4.5 + 3.7 + 3.1 + 3.8 + 3.4) \\div 6 = 3.5\\)","part":"(a)(i)"},{"for":"calculate \\((x - \\bar{x})^2\\)","shows":"\\(1, 1, 0.04, 0.16, 0.09, 0.01\\)","part":"(a)(ii)"},{"for":"substitute into formula","shows":"\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{2.3}{6 - 1}}\\)","part":"(a)(ii)"},{"for":"calculate standard deviation","shows":"\\(0.678\\ldots\\)","part":"(a)(ii)"},{"for":"comment regarding mean","shows":"eg on average weights in 2017 are higher","part":"(b)"},{"for":"comment regarding standard deviation","shows":"eg the weights in 2017 are more consistent","part":"(b)"},{"for":"4 points correct","shows":"evidence","part":"(c)(i)"},{"for":"all 8 points correct","shows":"evidence","part":"(c)(i)"},{"for":"consistent line of best fit","shows":"evidence","part":"(c)(ii)"},{"for":"answer consistent with line of best fit","shows":"evidence","part":"(c)(iii)"},{"for":"identify correct row in table","shows":"eg 8 (scoops)","part":"(d)"},{"for":"calculate milk powder needed for 1 week or equivalent","shows":"\\(4 \\times 8 \\times 7 \\times 4.5 = 1008\\), or \\(4.5 \\times 4 \\times 8 = 144\\) and \\(900 \\div 144 = 6.25\\)","part":"(d)"},{"for":"conclusion consistent with working","shows":"No (as 1008g > 900g), or No (as 6.25 < 7 days)","part":"(d)"}],"notes":["(a) 1. (ii) The alternative strategy's •² is calculate \\(\\sum x\\) and \\(\\sum x^2\\).","(a) 2. (ii) Correct answer with no working, award 0/3.","(a) 3. (ii) Accept rounding or truncation to at least one decimal place for final answer.","(a) 4. (ii) •⁴ can only be awarded for a calculation involving at least two steps including a division and a square root.","(c) 1. (i) The points, length then weight: 46, 2.7; 47, 2.8; 49, 3.5; 51, 3.7; 52, 3.4; 52, 3.7; 54, 4.0; 55, 4.4.","(c) 2. (iii) When the weight falls between 2 divisions accept either number or any value in between.","(d) 1. For •¹³ the comparison has to be grams with grams, days with days or scoops with scoops."]},
  "2019 P2 Q8": {"marks":6,"subject":"Lines and gaps along a bridge; two cables by Pythagoras.","rows":[{"for":"identify number of gaps","shows":"\\(366\\)","part":"(a)"},{"for":"calculate length","shows":"\\(366 \\times 2 + 367 \\times 4 = 2200\\)","part":"(a)"},{"for":"correct substitution in Pythagoras' Theorem","shows":"eg \\(300^2 - 295^2\\)","part":"(b)"},{"for":"calculate height or height²","shows":"\\(h = 54.5\\ldots\\) or \\(h^2 = 2975\\)","part":"(b)"},{"for":"correct substitution in Pythagoras' Theorem","shows":"\\(600^2 + (54.5\\ldots)^2\\)","part":"(b)"},{"for":"calculate total length of cable","shows":"\\(300 + 602.4\\ldots = 902.4\\ldots\\)","part":"(b)"}],"notes":["(b) 1. •³ is not available if candidate writes \\(295^2 - 300^2\\).","(b) 2. •⁴ is available if candidate writes \\(295^2 - 300^2\\) leading to \\(54.5\\ldots\\)","(b) 3. Do not penalise candidates who truncate or round to the nearest whole number throughout."]},
