  "2022 P1 Q7": {"marks":3,"subject":"An average gradient as a fraction in its simplest form, after matching units.","rows":[{"for":"calculate the correct vertical distance","shows":"\\(399\\) (m) or \\(0.399\\) (km)"},{"for":"state gradient","shows":"\\(\\frac{399}{3000}\\) or \\(\\frac{0.399}{3}\\)"},{"for":"express gradient as a fraction in its simplest form","shows":"\\(\\frac{133}{1000}\\)"}],"notes":["1. Correct answer with no working, award 3/3.","2. •² is only available for a denominator of 3 or 3000 where the units are consistent with the numerator.","3. •³ is not available when an attempt is made to further simplify a fraction already in its simplest form, eg \\(\\frac{133}{1000} = \\frac{66.5}{500}\\)."]},
  "2022 P1 Q8": {"marks":3,"subject":"The pizza left from two fractions of two pizzas.","rows":[{"for":"evidence of common denominator","shows":"evidence of \\(21\\) or equivalent"},{"for":"add fractions","shows":"\\(\\frac{29}{21}\\)"},{"for":"calculate the fraction that Jessica ate","shows":"\\(\\left(\\frac{42}{21} - \\frac{29}{21} =\\right) \\frac{13}{21}\\)"}],"notes":["1. The alternative strategy's skills: •¹ calculate the remaining fraction of each pizza; •² evidence of common denominator; •³ calculate the fraction that Jessica ate.","2. Correct answer with no working, award 3/3.","3. In original strategy, •³ is only available when the numerator is calculated by subtracting from 42.","4. In the alternative strategy, •³ is only available for adding the 2 fractions from •¹.","5. The final answer does not need to be in its simplest form.","6. Do not penalise incorrect simplification of final answer.","7. Candidates working in decimals must work to at least 3 decimal places for •² to be awarded in original strategy or •³ in alternative strategy.","8. Candidates working in percentages must work to at least 1 decimal place for •² to be awarded in original strategy or •³ in alternative strategy."]},
