  "2022 P1 Q11": {"marks":4,"subject":"The area of an isosceles triangle with a rectangle on top, via Pythagoras.","rows":[{"for":"correct substitution into Pythagoras' Theorem","shows":"\\(13^2 - 5^2\\)"},{"for":"calculate height of triangle","shows":"\\(12\\)"},{"for":"calculate area of triangle","shows":"\\((0.5 \\times 10 \\times 12 =)\\ 60\\)"},{"for":"calculate area of rectangle and add to area of triangle and state correct units","shows":"\\((10 \\times 4 + 60 =)\\ 100\\ \\text{cm}^2\\)"}],"notes":["1. Correct answer with no working, award 0/4.","2. For •⁴ correct units must be stated in final answer.","3. 12 with no working: •¹ and •² can be awarded.","4. •³ is only available for using a height, with the exceptions of \\(0.5 \\times 10 \\times 13 + 10 \\times 4 = 105\\ \\text{cm}^2\\) (awarded 2/4) and \\(0.5 \\times 10 \\times 13 = 65\\) (awarded 1/4).","5. •⁴ is only available for adding 40 \\((10 \\times 4)\\) to a previously **calculated** area."]},
