  "2023 P2 Q5": {"marks":9,"subject":"Mean and standard deviation, two comparisons, and a finishing time from inverse proportion.","rows":[{"for":"calculate mean","shows":"\\(2\\)","part":"(a)(i)"},{"for":"calculate \\((x - \\bar{x})^2\\)","shows":"\\(1.44, 0.01, 0.81, 0.36, 1.21, 0.16, 0.01\\)","part":"(a)(ii)"},{"for":"calculate \\(\\sum(x - \\bar{x})^2\\) and substitute into formula","shows":"\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{7 - 1}}\\)","part":"(a)(ii)"},{"for":"calculate standard deviation","shows":"\\(0.816\\ldots\\)","part":"(a)(ii)"},{"for":"comment regarding mean","shows":"eg on average, Colin's hot tub chlorine levels are higher","part":"(b)"},{"for":"comment regarding standard deviation","shows":"eg Stuart's hot tub chlorine levels are more consistent","part":"(b)"},{"for":"calculate number of hours for one worker","shows":"\\(48\\)","part":"(c)"},{"for":"calculate the decimal time for 5 workers","shows":"\\(9.6\\)","part":"(c)"},{"for":"convert decimal time and calculate finish time","shows":"18:06 or 6:06 pm","part":"(c)"}],"notes":["(a) 1. (ii) The alternative strategy's •² is calculate \\(\\sum x\\) and \\(\\sum x^2\\), and its •³ substitute into formula.","(a) 2. (ii) Correct answer without working, award 0/3.","(a) 3. (ii) Accept rounding or truncating to 1 decimal place for final answer.","(a) 4. (ii) For •³ do not penalise a square root sign that does not extend to the denominator.","(a) 5. (ii) •⁴ can only be awarded for a calculation involving at least 2 steps including a division and a square root.","(a) 6. (ii) •⁴ is not available if the denominator is 1, eg \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{2 - 1}} \\to 2\\) using the mean for n, awarded 1/3.","(b) 1. Answer must be consistent with answer to part (a).","(b) 2. Numerical comparisons are not required but when used they must be accurate.","(b) 3. For the award of •⁵, accept eg: on average, Colin's levels are higher; on average, Stuart's chlorine is lower; Stuart had a lower average chlorine level than Colin. Do not accept eg: on average Stuart is lower; Colin's levels are higher; Stuart's chlorine is lower; on average, the **mean** chlorine level was greater for Colin; on average, Colin's chlorine level was **better**; on average, Colin's hot tub is higher.","(b) 4. For the award of •⁶, accept eg: the levels in Stuart's hot tub are less varied; the levels in Colin's hot tub are less consistent; the chlorine in Colin's hot tub is more spread out; there is less variation in the chlorine levels in Stuart's hot tub. Do not accept eg: \"**On average**\" contained in any statement; Stuart's standard deviation is more consistent; the **range** of chlorine levels in Stuart's hot tub is less varied; Colin's hot tub is more varied.","(b) 5. \"On average, Stuart's chlorine levels are lower and **the levels** are more consistent\" is awarded 2/2; \"…lower and are more consistent\" is awarded 1/2.","(c) 1. Correct answer without working, award 3/3.","(c) 2. •⁹ is not available where a multiple of 0.5 hours or a whole number of hours is calculated for •⁸.","(c) 3. 18:06 pm with or without working is awarded 3/3; 18:06 am or 6:06 with or without working, 2/3."]},
